So, Arc is my 5th ascension.
Previously done Val, Wiz, Sam (loved that one!) and Mon (vegan, 
geno-poly-weaponless. Hard!)).

Thanks to all of you! Lurking (well, mostly lurking) r.g.r.n. makes 
nethack, if possible, even more rewarding!

Oh, !!!SPOILER WARNING!!!


I've recently played Pri, Ran and Rog to experience their quests - and 
then lost them due to boredom, I guess. Thinking hard about installing 
the Hell2 patch...

I had gotten so used to dying post-quest, I started to fear I had "lost 
it"... so I decided to do my best to ascended this one.

Started out without any special thoughts about conducts.
Early game consisted of Camaxtli throwing every Newtsmasher, 
Geckoknocker and lichenbane my way for #offering.

So, when a water demon on the Oracle level offered me a wish, I didn't 
hesitate to wish for Greyswandir... of course, with all the artifacts 
already in the game, I didn't get it :(
 From that point, I decided not to wish again. The RNG can keep his 
stupid speed boots, +oId etc!

In retrospect, I fully realize I should have been lawful to get 
Grayswandir from my god, but come on: Indy can't be lawful, he's badass!

In the quest, I tamed a horse and polytrapped him into a titan (/after/ 
killing The Minion; probably the closest call in the game).

I got speed boots in the castle and +oId from Molochs high priest himself.

My titan friend followed me through most of Gehennom before polytrapping 
himself into a Vampire, then I dithed him. Didn't find a single magic 
whistle in the game, so I was pretty tired of him anyway.

I forgot to bring ?oFD, and spent a looong time on the Planes.
Gave me time to meet plenty of archons - they're not that tough!

Finally standing on the high altar, I hung around for maybe 1500 turns 
more, but didn't find much of interest to do in the end (Famine kept 
coming after me, but Rodney never showed up again).
I realized it was too late to start planning any crazy conducts 
anyway... time to make Camaxtli happy.

Any ideas what would be fun to try next?


